\begin{align*}
    &\dfrac{s-t}{r-t}\div\dfrac{s-q}{r-q}\in\mathbb{R}
    =&\dfrac{      \left( \dfrac{2a+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}   \right)  -     \left( \dfrac{a-\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}  \right)    }{  \left(   \dfrac{a+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{3}}}{3} \right)- \left( \dfrac{a-\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}\right)}\div\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{2a+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}\right)-\left(\dfrac{\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}\right)}{\left(\dfrac{a+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}\right)-\left(\dfrac{\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}}}{3}\right)}
    =&\dfrac{(a+\sqrt{3})(a\sqrt{3}+1)}{8a}
.\end{align*}

Taking the conjugate of this term and using  $\overline{a}=\dfrac{1}{a}$  shows that it equals its conjugate and so its a real value and we are done.

