We will show that, regardless of what numbers Tsvety puts in the shaded squares, there is at most one way to fill the rest of the infinite grid.

From hereon, assume that  $m > n$ . Firstly, Freyja can determine each number in the  $(n-1) \times (m-n)$  rectangle in the top right corner, starting from the bottom left:
