where  $P$  and  $Q$  are integers summing to  $n$  and  $S$  and  $T$  are integers summing to  $m$ . Since  $m$  and  $n$  are coprime, it follows that  $\tfrac{P}{Q} \neq \tfrac{S}{T}$ , so this system of equations has exactly one solution. We can find the other variables in terms of  $a_m$  and  $a_n$ .

Now, Freyja has determined one more row – she can repeat this process to determine the numbers in an infinitely tall strip of width  $m+n-2$ . Now she does this same process sideways to fill in the whole grid.
