Now the  $2n+2$  odd-indexed coins must then be flipped at least  $4n+1$  times to keep up with the even indexed flips. But since each odd indexed coin must be flipped an odd number of times and there are an even number of them, we get that they must be flipped atlesat  $4n+2$  times.

Group the coins into the following bunches   $$ \boxed{TH}\underbrace{\boxed{THTH}\boxed{THTH}\dots \boxed{THTH}}_{505}\boxed{T} $$   Now in the first group, apply the following operation(the coin that is going to get flipped is underlined).  $$ T\underline{H}\rightarrow \underline{T}T\rightarrow H\underline{T}\rightarrow HH $$   so in the next move we can start with the first coin of the second group. Now inductivley apply the following transformation:
\begin{align*}
