\[m=\frac{p+q}{2}\]
Since the desired result is that points  $O$  ,  $M$  and  $H$  are collinear, it suffices to show that  $\frac{m-o}{h-o} \in \mathbb{R}$ . We first compute  $\frac{m-o}{h-o}$ .
