Redefine  $N$  to be the intersection of  $AQ$  with the perpendicular line from  $M$  to  $BC$ . We wish to show that  $AN=NQ$ .

Make the observation that
\[\angle AMN=90^\circ - \angle AMB = 90^\circ - \angle CMP = \angle MCP.\]
Therefore,
\[\frac{AN}{NQ}=\frac{AM}{MQ}\frac{\sin \angle AMN}{\sin \angle NMQ} = \frac{BM}{MP}\sin \angle AMN = \frac{CM}{MP}\sin \angle MCP = 1.\]

