[/asy]
Then, put all the red numbers on the circle in increasing clockwise order and put all the blue numbers on the circle in increasing clockwise order. This results in everything being sorted!

To conclude, the expected number of moves in the first step is, by Lemma 1,  $$ \frac{1}{2}\left(2\left({25\choose 2} + {25\choose 2}\right) + 25^2 + 2\left({25\choose 2} + {24\choose 2}\right) + 25\cdot 24\right) = 1788.5, $$  while the the expected number of moves in the second step is, by Lemma 2,  $$ \frac{1}{2}\cdot \left(25^2 + 25\cdot 24\right) = 612.5. $$  By linearity of expectation, the expected total moves is  $2401$ , so one of these choices requires at most  $2401$  moves.  $\blacksquare$

