\frac{\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{y}+\sqrt{z}+3\epsilon}{3}&=\frac{2}{3}n
\implies\left|\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{y}+\sqrt{z}-2\sqrt{N}\right|&\ll2023.
\end{align*}
If there is a leftover tile in the center, its label is  $\lfloor\tfrac{2}{3}n\rfloor^2+\lfloor\tfrac{2}{3}n\rfloor+1$ , which can be verified to be a valid single.

