This is the main lemma.**<span style="color:#00f">Lemma: </span>**If  $p \ge 2027$  is a prime then for any  $e \ge 1$ ,  $p \nmid m$  and  $a \in \mathbb N$  we have \[p^e  \mid a^{2^{mp^e}}-a \implies p^e \mid \sum_{k=1}^{mp^e} k^{2024}a^{2^k}\] **Proof:** See that if  $p \mid a$  then  $p^e \mid a$  and so we are done anyways. So assume  $p \nmid a$ . 

Now let  $d$  be the smallest number for which  $\text{ord}_p(a) \mid 2^d-1$  and see that if  $\text{ord}_p(a) \mid 2^N-1 \iff d \mid N$ . So we have  $d \mid mp^e$ . 

Also  $a^{2^k} \equiv a^{2^\ell} \pmod p \iff d \mid k-\ell$ . This implies that  $a^{2^k}$  is periodic modulo  $p$  with period  $d$  and hence if  $d \ge p$ , then  $a^2$ ,  $a^{2^2}$ ,  $\dots$ ,  $a^{2^p}$  forms a complete residue system modulo  $p$  so one of them is divisible by  $p$ , contradiction. Hence  $d<p$  and in particular  $p \nmid d$  and so  $d \mid m$ . 

Now to the actual thing. We will induct on  $e$ . We will work in  $\mathbb{F}_p$  the whole time. \begin{align*}
\sum_{k=1}^{mp} k^{2024}a^{2^k} &= \sum_{k=1}^d a^{2^k} \left [k^{2024}+(k+d)^{2024}+\dots+\left(k+\left(\frac{mp}d-1 \right) d \right)^{2024} \right ] 
&= \sum_{k=1}^d a^{2^k} \sum_{i=0}^{2024} k^{2024-i} \binom{2024}i d^i \underbrace{\sum_{\ell=0}^{\frac{mp}d-1} \ell^i}_{=0} 
&=0
\end{align*} Now assume it is true for  $e$ , we will prove it for  $e+1$ . We actually want to prove that \[p^e \mid \sum_{k=1}^{mp^e} k^{2024}a^{2^k} \implies p^{e+1} \mid \sum_{k=1}^{mp^{e+1}} k^{2024}a^{2^k}\] Work in  $\mathbb{Z}/p^{e+1}\mathbb{Z}$ . \begin{align*}
\sum_{k=1}^{mp^{e+1}} k^{2024}a^{2^k} &= \sum_{k=1}^{mp^e} a^{2^k} \sum_{\ell=0}^{p-1} (k+\ell mp^e)^{2024} 
&= \sum_{k=1}^{mp^e} a^{2^k} \sum_{\ell=0}^{p-1} \sum_{i=0}^{2024} k^{2024-i} (m\ell)^i p^{ei} \binom{2024}i 
&= \sum_{k=1}^{mp^e} a^{2^k} \sum_{\ell=0}^{p-1} k^{2024}+k^{2023} \ell mp^e \cdot 2024 
&= p \sum_{k=1}^{mp^e} a^{2^k} k^{2024} 
&= 0 
\end{align*} So we are done with the induction hypothesis.  $\square$ This obviously implies the problem.

