ilarly,  $$ q = \frac{dz}{2d-z} = -\frac{ef}{d} $$  Also,  $$ m = \frac{y+z}2 = \frac{d(de+df-4ef)}{2(d^2-ef)} $$  Now we just have to find the coordinate of  $R$ . Now let  $AP, KQ$  meet the unit circle again at  $A', K'$  respectively. Then  $$ a' = \frac{p-a}{p\overline{a}-1} = \frac{d(de+df-2ef)}{2d-e-f} = d $$  (That is,  $A, D, P$  are collinear.) And  $$ k' = \frac{q-k}{q\overline{k}-1} = \frac{ef(d^2+de+df-ef)}{d(de+df+ef-d^2)} $$  Then
