 \frac{(138-k)(144+k)}{4}&\leq a_{k+2}\leq \frac{(138-k)(146+k)}{4} 
\end{align*}

Thus, this is always possible for all even nonnegative integer  $n\leq 138$ . 

Then, after Penny does it repeatedly until  $n=138$ ,  $140\leq a_{138}\leq 141$ . Realize that, since  $1\leq a_{139}\leq 140$ , Penny can take all the stones remaining at the  $140$ th turn.
